    {
        "content": "<p>The following is a <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mwe.html\">#mwe</a> of a situation in my larger project. I have a series of operations on structures with a raw data field, and a wellformedness field that contains a structure of propositions. Explicitly passing the structure's field name solves the goal, so I've tried to see whether I could make simp annotations do the same. However even using <code>attribute [simp] &lt;structure fields&gt;</code> doesn't make <code>simp</code> use them automatically. Is there a proper way to go about this?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Circuit</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Raw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">dom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">adj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Raw</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">size</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Raw</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">dom</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Node</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Raw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">outputIds</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Raw</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getNode</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Raw</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Node</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Raw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">outputIds</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">range</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">filter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">adj</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">adj</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Node</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Raw</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">WFNodeOf</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Node</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Raw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Circuit</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Raw</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">outputIds_lt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">outputIds</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">size</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Raw</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">WF</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Circuit</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Raw</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">size_wf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">dom</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">adj</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">nodes_wf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">size</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getNode</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">WFNodeOf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">root_</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Circuit</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Circuit</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Raw</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">wf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">WF</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">size</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Circuit</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">size</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Node</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Circuit</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">size</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Node</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Raw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">id</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">wf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">WFNodeOf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">raw</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Node</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">outputIds</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Node</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">outputIds</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mythm</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Circuit</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">idx</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">xnode</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Node</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">idx</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xnode</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">outputIds</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">size</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">simp_all</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">xnode</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wf</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">outputIds_lt</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- works</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- simp_all --fails even when using `attribute [simp] ...` commands on `Node` and `Node.Raw.WFNodeOf`</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 595906459,
        "sender_full_name": "nrs",
        "timestamp": 1779129565
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Try adding <code>attribute [simp] Node.Raw.WFNodeOf.outputIds_lt</code></p>",
        "id": 595923218,
        "sender_full_name": "Yury G. Kudryashov",
        "timestamp": 1779133869
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I've been trying a couple of combinations of the <code>attribute</code> command including that one but for some reason it doesn't work unfortunately. I'm wondering, this is a possibly expected use case of <code>simp</code> right? The reason I'm thinking this should work is that, supposing we organize a code around some <code>MyType</code> which is a combination of <code>MyType.Raw</code> and <code>MyType.WF</code> (following the lead of <code>Std.DHashMap</code> &amp; cie),  proofs involving a wellformed term of a raw structure (i.e., a term of a structure containing one structure for raw data and one structure for wellformedness properties) will always boil down to a usage of the wellformedness properties, no? So we'd expect simp to be able to acquire the fields of <code>MyType.WF</code> from <code>MyType</code></p>",
        "id": 595926205,
        "sender_full_name": "nrs",
        "timestamp": 1779134819
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think explicitly writing very small theorems providing the projections is a work-around, but I was wondering whether there was a more automatic approach</p>",
        "id": 595926460,
        "sender_full_name": "nrs",
        "timestamp": 1779134913
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The problem is that the theorem <code>outputIdx_lt</code> matches on <code>id &lt; c.size</code> and it has no way of figuring which <code>x</code> to use.</p>",
        "id": 595927770,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1779135383
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You'd need some kind of forward reasoning to deduce the specific instantiation of <code>outputIds_lt</code> from the presence of a <code>Node</code> which <code>grind</code> can do but <code>simp</code> can't so easily</p>",
        "id": 595928096,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1779135483
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hm I see, in this specific case, we can use</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">attribute</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Node</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Raw</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">WFNodeOf</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">outputIds_lt</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">attribute</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">grind!</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Node</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wf</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I'm not too sure whether this is a recommended usage for <code>grind</code>, in general I'm a bit confused how many/where should simp/grind attributes go, and whether to use <code>grind</code> or <code>simp</code> attributes for specific cases. For instance, <code>grind</code> works for this case, but does the fact <code>simp</code> doesn't work indicate that I should proceed with <code>grind</code> or that my code isn't correctly structured?</p>\n<p>EDIT: annotating your structures with <code>@[grind]</code> and more specifically <code>@[grind cases]</code> will automatically add their contents to <code>grind</code>'s set of equivalence classes and True/False props</p>",
        "id": 595930505,
        "sender_full_name": "nrs",
        "timestamp": 1779136315
    }
]